\title{SAINTexpress: Pure R Implementation of SAINTexpress}
\description{
Scores bait-prey interactions in affinity purification-mass spectrometry
(AP-MS) experiments with the SAINTexpress model (Teo et al. 2014). For each
prey detected in the purification of a bait, SAINT compares the prey's
spectral counts or intensities in the bait purifications with those in
negative-control purifications and returns the probability that the
interaction is genuine.
}
\details{
The package reimplements the spectral-count (\code{SAINTexpress-spc}) and
intensity (\code{SAINTexpress-int}) engines of the native C++ SAINTexpress 3.6.3
in R. Its output has the columns of the native \code{list.txt} file.

Main functions:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=run_saint]{run_saint()}} scores a SAINT input list.
\item \code{\link[=validate_saint_input]{validate_saint_input()}} checks a SAINT input list before scoring.
}

A subset of the real AP-MS dataset TIP49 (the example shipped with
SAINTexpress) and the native SAINTexpress 3.6.3 results for it are in
\code{inst/extdata/tip49}; see the vignette.
}
\references{
